# Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# THIS FILE WINS over a real environment variable. Setting a shell variable will
# NOT override a line here: the home's .env is the single place that decides, so an
# export you have forgotten about cannot quietly change which key a run uses.
# (harness.infra.home/env-source owns that order, and the settings panel reports
# which of the two a key actually came from.)
#
# ONE KEY PER PROVIDER, named after its id: the id uppercased with anything that is
# not a letter or a digit turned into an underscore, plus _API_KEY.
#
#   :openrouter    ->  OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   :acme-gateway  ->  ACME_GATEWAY_API_KEY
#
# A provider's own line beats the global one below, and the global one is the
# fallback for everything that does not have a line of its own -- the three
# built-in vendors, an inline description in config.edn, a provider you added
# before this rule existed. So a home with only this line keeps working.
HARNESS_API_KEY=sk-replace-me

# A second provider, with its own key. Uncomment and rename to match your
# config.edn's :providers entry:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-replace-me
